# Teach skill output lives in `learn/`

When running the `/teach` skill (or creating MISSION, NOTES, RESOURCES, lessons, assets, reference, or learning-records), **root the teaching workspace at `learn/`**, not the repo root.

| Teach skill default | This repo |
| --- | --- |
| `MISSION.md` | `learn/MISSION.md` |
| `NOTES.md` | `learn/NOTES.md` |
| `RESOURCES.md` | `learn/RESOURCES.md` |
| `./lessons/*.html` | `learn/lessons/*.html` |
| `./assets/*` | `learn/assets/*` |
| `./reference/*.html` | `learn/reference/*.html` |
| `./learning-records/*.md` | `learn/learning-records/*.md` |

Create `learn/` (and subfolders) if they do not exist. Do not write those files at the repo root. Do not mix teaching files with app source (`lib/`, `components/`, `app/`).

Relative links inside lessons stay one level up from the lesson file, e.g. `learn/lessons/0001-….html` → `../assets/lesson.css`.

```
# ❌ BAD — teach files at repo root
lessons/0001-two-keys.html
MISSION.md

# ✅ GOOD — same files under learn/
learn/lessons/0001-two-keys.html
learn/MISSION.md
```
